course: dictionary
lesson: 11300
title: One word, many meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning. Yard is one of them. To find the right meaning, read the words around it, which are its context. «One yard is 3 feet, and one foot is 12 inches.» Here yard is a measure of length, like a metre.
explain: «A plan is a detailed map of a small place, such as a room or a school yard.» Here a yard is an open area for play or work, not a measure. Ask yourself: does the sentence talk about how long something is, or about a place? That question solves most cases.
explain: Place yard is more than one meaning, so always test your choice. Swap your meaning into the sentence. If «school yard» became «school unit of length», it makes no sense, so the place meaning is right.
fact: Context means the words and sentences around a word.
fact: A yard is a unit of length. One yard is 3 feet, or 36 inches.
fact: A yard can also be the ground around a house. In the USA this often has grass, but in the UK people usually call it a «garden».
fact: A yard can be an open area for work or play, as in «school yard», «farmyard» or «shipyard».
fact: In American football the attack has 4 downs to gain 10 yards.
exercise: «One yard is 3 feet, and one foot is 12 inches.» How many inches is one yard? | *36 | 12 | 48 | 24
exercise: «A plan is a detailed map of a small place, such as a room or a school yard.» In this sentence, what is a yard? | A unit of length | A kind of bridge | A type of ferry-boat | *An open area for play
exercise: «First he hopped one yard; then he hopped three yards.» What is a yard measuring here? | A school field | A river bank | *A unit of length | A kind of hop
test: «Drive a remote-control car only in the yard, park or a quiet path, never in the street.» Why must the car stay out of the street? | Streets are made of grass | The car is too fast for the park | *You might run after it into traffic | It might rain
test: In American football, a touchdown is 6 points, and the attack has 4 downs to gain 10 yards. How many yards must the attack gain? | *10 | 3 | 6 | 4
exam: In the USA, the back yard usually has grass. What do British people call that grassy ground behind a house? | Street | *Garden | Park | Field
